This product includes software developed by Vadym Chernets, as part of Poly A1.

Ported from the author's own V1 project (not published), with its tests' ideas:
- packages/mail-digest/source-imap.mjs - IMAP read-only by the protocol: EXAMINE with a
  confirmed [READ-ONLY], a whitelist of commands on the wire, BODY.PEEK only, \Seen measured
  before and after.
- packages/mail-digest/alerts-links.mjs - Google Alerts links taken by code, not by a model:
  redirect unwrapping, tracker cutting, Google's own links dropped, the sender vouched for by the
  receiving server (Authentication-Results by mx.google.com).
- packages/core-poly/morning-council/claude-mail-digest.mjs - the digest's threat model (a letter
  can be written for the AI; its text is data, never an instruction) and the closed list of labels.

Public references:
- RFC 3501 (IMAP4rev1), sections 6.3.2 (EXAMINE) and 6.4.5 (BODY.PEEK does not set \Seen).
- Google Alerts, https://www.google.com/alerts - delivery to mail or to an RSS feed.
- Gmail connector for Claude, https://claude.com/connectors/gmail
